{"name":"Flamingo","hex":"#e1634f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flamingo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wading bird of the family Phoenicopteridae of the order Phoenicopteriformes.","A deep pink color tinged with orange, like that of a flamingo."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep pink color tinged with orange, like that of a flamingo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flamingo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flamingo","blocks":[{"text":"Flamingos or flamingoes are a type of wading bird in the family Phoenicopteridae, which is the only extant family in the order Phoenicopteriformes. There are four flamingo species distributed throughout the Americas, and two species native to Afro-Eurasia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Flamingos_Laguna_Colorada.jpg/330px-Flamingos_Laguna_Colorada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flamingo"},{"title":"Flamingo (Brandon Flowers album)","blocks":[{"text":"Flamingo is the debut solo studio album by American singer-songwriter Brandon Flowers, frontman of rock group the Killers, released on September 3, 2010, by Island Records. The album incorporates elements of soft rock and country pop, departing from the dance-rock and new wave influences of the Killers' 2008 studio album Day & Age. Produced by Flowers, Daniel Lanois, Brendan O'Brien, and Stuart Price, Flamingo features musicians such as Rilo Kiley frontwoman Jenny Lewis, fellow Killers members Dave Keuning and Ronnie Vannucci Jr., and guitarist Benji Lysaght."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c8/Brandon_Flowers_-_Flamingo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flamingo_(Brandon_Flowers_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Flamingo_range.png/500px-Flamingo_